  "notes": "Registered before the run. A robustness replication of personal-study-3's S&P 500 timing methods and the adopted sso-trend200 (with its 1x twin) on the Kenneth R. French Data Library's daily market and T-bill returns since July 1926: the methods are unchanged, nothing is fitted, and no new trial is counted. HOLDS_UP needs all of: excess log growth over the market above 0 over the whole history; ahead of the market in at least 6 of the 9 complete decades (1930s-2010s); maximum drawdown at most 10 points worse than the market's; ahead in at least 60% of rolling 10-year windows; excess above 0 after its publication (from the January after the year listed); and excess above 0 at 20 bps a side. HOLDS_UP_PARTLY: whole-history excess above 0 but another test failed. Otherwise DOES_NOT_HOLD_UP. Trading at the signal's own close, Holm over the five replications and the calendar-year extremes are reported, not tested. KNOWN_HISTORY: the forward record of the alerts is the test.",
